==Icelandic==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ˈmaːðʏr]|lang=is}}
*: {{audio|Is-maður.ogg|Audio (Iceland, Kópavogur)}}
*: {{rhymes|aːðʏr|lang=is}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|maðr}}.

===Noun===
{{is-noun|m|manns|menn}}

# a [[man]], a [[human being]]{{jump|is|human being|s}}
#: ''Það tilheyrir náttúru '''mannsins''' að hata þá sem hann hefur sært.''
#:: It belongs to '''human''' nature to hate those that he has hurt.
# {{context|mainly used with a definite article}} a [[husband]]{{jump|is|husband|s}}
#: ''[[þetta|Þetta]] er [[Geir]], '''maðurinn''' [[minn]].''
#:: This is Geir, [[my]] '''husband'''.
# a [[chessman]]{{jump|is|chessman|s}}
#: ''[[færa|Færðu]] '''manninn''' [[þinn]].''
#:: [[move|Move]] [[your]] '''chessman'''.

